WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.327 --> 00:00:07.709
There are at least 11 trillion reasons to worry about what Joe Biden wants to do to our economy and freedoms.

00:00:07.709 --> 00:00:11.293
He campaigned on a platform that the Washington Post called

00:00:11.293 --> 00:00:15.195
“more liberal than that of every past democratic nominee”.

00:00:15.195 --> 00:00:20.778
He’s bad news not just for the economy but for a wide range of libertarian concerns,

00:00:20.778 --> 00:00:26.088
such as school choice, individual autonomy, and the First and Second Amendments.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.088 --> 00:00:31.209
When Biden warned in the last presidential debate that we’re entering a "dark winter,"

00:00:31.209 --> 00:00:38.868
he was referring to Covid-19, but its his policies that are most likely to keep us stuck at home and out of work.

00:00:38.868 --> 00:00:44.054
Biden is proposing 11 trillion dollars in brand-new spending over the coming decade. 

00:00:44.054 --> 00:00:49.588
Among his biggest-ticket items are 1.4 trillion dollars to expand Obamacare;

00:00:49.588 --> 00:00:52.925
2 trillion dollars for his version of the Green New Deal; 

00:00:52.925 --> 00:00:58.810
1 trillion dollars in new Social Security and Supplemental Security Income spending;

00:00:58.810 --> 00:01:05.249
 and 1.5 trillion more dollars for preschool, K-12 and higher education.

00:01:05.249 --> 00:01:12.865
He has also signed on to a 3.3 trillion dollars stimulus spending plan pushed by House and Senate Democrats.

00:01:12.865 --> 00:01:22.152
That all comes after nearly 7 trillion dollars in federal spending this past year, up from a then-record 4.4 trillion dollars in 2019. 

00:01:22.152 --> 00:01:29.229
To pay for this new largess, Biden has laid out 3.6 trillion dollars in tax hikes over the coming decade,

00:01:29.229 --> 00:01:32.971
resulting in what the Manhattan Institute’s Brian Riedl calls

00:01:32.971 --> 00:01:36.917
"the largest permanent tax increase since World War II." 

00:01:36.917 --> 00:01:41.456
But Biden’s spending plan as laid out in his campaign is so out of control

00:01:41.456 --> 00:01:44.727
that he would still manage to increase the national debt

00:01:44.727 --> 00:01:52.180
by about 5.6 trillion dollars by 2030, according to the Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget.

00:01:52.180 --> 00:02:00.502
Just as scary are Biden’s seemingly infinite promises to push new government controls into virtually all aspects of our lives. 

00:02:00.502 --> 00:02:06.518
He wants to repeal Section 230, the law that protects online platforms from legal liability

00:02:06.518 --> 00:02:08.666
for speech generated by users,

00:02:08.666 --> 00:02:14.566
and he wants to "take a really hard look" at breaking up tech companies, especially Facebook.&nbsp;

00:02:14.566 --> 00:02:21.521
He's called for an end to federal funding for charter schools and the reinstatement of ineffective assault-weapons bans,

00:02:21.521 --> 00:02:24.137
and countless other gun-control measures.

00:02:24.137 --> 00:02:30.432
Pick any page of his campaign website's extensive "vision" section and you'll find endless proposals

00:02:30.432 --> 00:02:35.153
to tinker with virtually all aspects of everyday life and employment. 

00:02:35.153 --> 00:02:41.070
He pledges to "aggressively” regulate all contractual agreements between employees and employers, 

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:43.449
especially those in the gig economy,

00:02:43.449 --> 00:02:50.110
and he wants to "establish an Environmental and Climate Justice Division within the U.S. Department of Justice."

00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:58.412
In "Joe's Agenda for Students," he promises to require "aggressive methane pollution limits for oil and gas operations" 

00:02:58.412 --> 00:03:03.214
while also making "four-year public colleges and universities tuition-free

00:03:03.214 --> 00:03:08.918
 for all students whose family incomes are below $125,000."

00:03:08.918 --> 00:03:15.483
Biden was a punchline for much of his half-century in the public eye because of his constant gaffes and scandals

00:03:15.483 --> 00:03:20.000
but he is also a battle-hardened politician whose time has finally come.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:27.089
Joe Biden’s season in the sun comes nearly 50 years after he first entered national politics,

00:03:27.089 --> 00:03:33.020
and he may well usher in a dark winter that will persist long after next spring's bloom.

